            <div xml:id="d810">

                <pb facs="0820" n="702" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg702"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.154/66</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-10-05">October 5, 1929</date>.<lb/>[Received October
                        9.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1180</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my telegram No. 239,
                    September 30 (11 a.m.), concerning the Department’s wishes with respect to the
                    attitude of Commander Warfield in the matter of a road construction program in
                        <pb facs="0821" n="703" xml:id="pg703"/> Nicaragua, I have the honor to
                    transmit herewith a copy of Commander Warfield’s preliminary report which he has
                    submitted to the Legation in response to the Department’s wishes.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Matthew E. Hanna</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d810-a1.xml" xpointer="d810-a1"/>
            </div>
